cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software itself and the
  associated paper (see `preferred-citation`).
title: >-
  pol-predictors-2026: benchmarking of in-silico pathogenicity predictors in the
  POLE and POLD1 exonuclease domains
abstract: >-
  Analysis code reproducing every figure and table of the manuscript "AlphaMissense
  shows improved performance for predicting the pathogenicity of POLE and POLD1
  exonuclease domain variants". Evaluates six missense pathogenicity predictors
  (REVEL, AlphaMissense, BayesDel, CADD, PrimateAI and PrimateAI-3D) on a
  Pathogenic/Benign control set, on variants of uncertain significance and on gnomAD
  variants of the POLE and POLD1 exonuclease domains, using the published
  ClinGen-calibrated PP3/BP4 thresholds.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ValleLab-IDIBELL/pol-predictors-2026"
keywords:
  - POLE
  - POLD1
  - exonuclease domain
  - variant classification
  - in-silico pathogenicity predictors
  - AlphaMissense
  - REVEL
  - ACMG/AMP
  - ClinGen
  - PP3/BP4
